{{- /*
model.door.recover — the crash seam, as the harness carries it.

Rendered into the harness generator's fields region. A constructor over
the PRIOR instance rather than over the subject, because the medium
belongs to the instance: every check runs in parallel and owns its own
world, so a recovery constructor with nothing but the subject to go on
could only reopen a world it shares with everybody else.

The pair mirrors New and Start for the same reason those are a pair:
reopening a real medium usually wants the test's lifetime to clean up
after.
*/ -}}
{{- define "model.door.recover" -}}
	// Recover builds the process again over the medium the prior instance
	// left behind — no Close first, because a crash is the goodbye that
	// never happens. Checks that kill the process need it, and fail
	// naming this field when it is nil. StartRecover is its Start-shaped
	// sibling, for a reopen that also needs the test's lifetime; set at
	// most one of the two.
	//
	// If your implementation keeps everything in memory, it has no medium
	// to recover and this is the wrong answer: list the check in Excuse
	// instead, which reports it as excused rather than as passed.
	Recover      func(prior T) T
	StartRecover func(tb {{ renderExpr (external "testing" "TB") }}, prior T) T
{{- end -}}
